[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3328001303","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/110824#issuecomment-3328001303","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/110824","id":3328001303,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7GXUUX","user":{"login":"mihe","id":4884246,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ4ODQyNDY=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4884246?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe","html_url":"https://github.com/mihe","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-09-24T11:42:24Z","updated_at":"2025-09-24T11:54:49Z","body":"Seeing as how the shaking goes away when disabling the `physics/common/physics_interpolation` project setting, I'm guessing it might have something to do with #104269?\n\nI'm unfortunately not very well acquainted with the gotchas of the physics interpolation, so I'm not sure what the fix would be in this case. Maybe you have some idea, @lawnjelly?\n\nEDIT: The regression did seem to happen between 4.5-dev3 and 4.5-dev4, so likely caused by #104269.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3328001303/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3328362965","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/110824#issuecomment-3328362965","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/110824","id":3328362965,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7GYsnV","user":{"login":"lawnjelly","id":21999379,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIxOTk5Mzc5","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/21999379?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly","html_url":"https://github.com/lawnjelly","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-09-24T13:13:22Z","updated_at":"2025-09-24T13:15:01Z","body":"I answered a question on discord about this just the other day.\n\nWe are aware, it's because the debug physics were interpolated in 4.4, and in 4.5 the debug physics are not interpolated (since `SceneTreeFTI`) and show the correct position of the actual physics. These will jitter as seen in the viewport as you are looking from an interpolated camera, but the physics is actually correct, 4.4 is in some sense \"incorrect\" as it gives you a false impression of where the physics is.\n\nNow, if by popular opinion we decide that just \"looking nicer\" trumps physically correct in this case..  we need to proceed with #104518 (or a variation) and then we can tell the debug physics to use this method (as debug physics doesn't use nodes, so can't use `SceneTreeFTI`).\n\nIn the short term, yeah it looks a bit weird, but it's not actually incorrect (or a bug _per se_) but we may decide to smooth it out.","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3328362965/reactions","total_count":2,"+1":2,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3441571896","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/110824#issuecomment-3441571896","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/110824","id":3441571896,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7NIjg4","user":{"login":"AndreaCatania","id":8342599,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgzNDI1OTk=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/8342599?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/AndreaCatania","html_url":"https://github.com/AndreaCatania","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AndreaCatania/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AndreaCatania/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AndreaCatania/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AndreaCatania/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AndreaCatania/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AndreaCatania/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AndreaCatania/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AndreaCatania/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AndreaCatania/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-10-24T07:40:52Z","updated_at":"2025-10-24T07:40:52Z","body":"Yeah, it looks very weird from the prospective of a game dev. Unless you have a specific reason, like debugging the physics to fix a simulation bug or such, it doesn't make sense to disable the interpolation. Having the option to turn it on / off would be more desirable IMH.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3441571896/reactions","total_count":2,"+1":2,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null}]